(Virtual Memory and Paging) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Virtual memory lets the operating system give each process its own large address space.) Tj T*
(The kernel divides memory into pages and uses a page table to translate addresses.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(When a process touches a page that is not in memory, a page fault occurs and the) Tj T*
(operating system loads the page from disk. Paging and segmentation both reduce) Tj T*
(fragmentation of memory.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Too many page faults slow the whole system down, a condition known as thrashing.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
